{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "sdk_root": "implementations/sdk",
  "comment": [
    "Public client surface every LCP SDK ships, one entry per language.",
    "Derived from the code in implementations/sdk/ at v1.2.0 (see tools/check_sdk_surface.py).",
    "`members.<sdk>.name` is the exact, case-sensitive identifier in `file`; `null`",
    "records a shipped gap: the operation exists in the protocol but that SDK does not",
    "expose it yet. Gaps are reported, not failed, unless --fail-on-gap is passed.",
    "Paths are relative to the SDK root; `file` is relative to implementations/sdk/<sdk>/.",
    "`behaviours` rows cover what a method name cannot show (retry, timeout, constant-time",
    "verify, contact hash). Each SDK lists `evidence`: files and the exact, case-sensitive",
    "substrings each must contain, the source primitive and the test that exercises it.",
    "`\"evidence\": null` records a gap, as `name: null` does for an operation."
  ],
